@100 = ~Allesia Faithhammer has asked us to investigate reports of a ghost haunting Hope's Haven.~
@101 = ~We discovered that the supposed haunting was caused by a Mourning Lace flower upstairs. The children should be safe now.~
@102 = ~Orphanage~
@103 = ~You have my word, Allesia. We will bring this matter to close. I cannot claim mastery over the rituals of exorcism, but I am not helpless against the undead. My training has taught me to recognise the signs of their presence and to confront such creatures without fear. Should this spirit manifest itself, I shall face it. If it can be destroyed by steel, I shall destroy it. If it requires divine power, I shall call upon Helm to aid me.~
@104 = ~Tempus teaches us to face danger, not to cower from it, and his priests are trained for battle, not for the rites by which spirits are driven from the mortal realm. I know well enough how to fight a creature of flesh and blood. A spirit, however, is another matter entirely. I suppose we shall see if we undertake the task.~
@105 = ~If there truly be a spirit hauntin’ this place, I’d need tae lay me eyes upon it afore I could say what ought tae be done. Some undead can be put down like any other creature, whilst others require the proper rites tae send ’em beyond this world. Best not tae go swingin’ at shadows until we ken what we’re dealin’ with.~
@106 = ~I possess certain abilities that might serve to disrupt or weaken a possession. Whether they would suffice to banish a spirit entirely is another question. And why should I concern myself with the safety of human children? Their troubles are hardly my concern. (sighs) Nevertheless... if you insist upon banishing this spirit, I would first need to see it for myself. Until I know what we are dealing with, any attempt to drive it out would be little more than guesswork.~
@107 = ~Welcome to Hope's Haven. My name is Allesia Faithhammer. What can I do for you?~
@108 = ~You're running this place all by yourself?~
@109 = ~Aren't you a little too young and adventurous to be an orphanage caretaker?~
@110 = ~You sound tense.~
@111 = ~Goodbye.~
@112 = ~Anything else you wonder about?~
@113 = ~You're running this place all by yourself?~
@114 = ~Aren't you a little too young and adventurous to be an orphanage caretaker?~
@115 = ~You sound tense.~
@116 = ~Goodbye.~
@117 = ~Yes. There are days when I wonder whether I've taken on more than I can reasonably handle. Then one of the children comes running to me with some little treasure they've found, or they learn something new, or they simply smile because they know they're safe... and I remember why I am here.~
@118 = ~I have devoted my life to serving Helm. My mentor always told me that I was destined for greatness. Being an orphanage caretaker may not be the sort of greatness that first comes to mind, but I have come to regard this work as my duty. And a sacred one at that.~
@119 = ~You're absolutely right, good paladin. Nasty times are upon us and we need to take care of one another, so benevolence overcomes malice.~
@120 = ~Heh. You're not the first and certainly not the last to say that. I joined the ranks of Helm priests to spread virtue and compassion and fight for a greater cause. Initially, orphanage wasn't handled by me but my high-ranking mentor - Huros. Since his duties lie elsewhere and he is needed more at the Church of Helm, I volunteered to overtake his work.~
@121 = ~My grand aspirations of travelling the world and aiding those in need transformed into another. I thought to myself, I can't help every person out there, but I can help orphaned children who lost their families. That gives me a sense of purpose no less profound than any grand adventure ever could.~
@122 = ~Am I that transparent (nervous laugh)? Well, I take pride in delivering these children into a better life, however my work has become more difficult as of late. One of the youngest girls, Mia has come to me recently and claimed she had seen a ghost. You know how impressionable kids are. I was afraid other kids invented some silly bedtime story to scare the younger ones. But I'm not so sure anymore.~
@123 = ~More and more children started coming forward and telling me about alleged ghost sighting. Each time I investigate, no evidence of ghostly apparitions is found. Helmites are explicitly trained in handling spiritual activities and in exorcisms. I have never encountered a spirit before but it is within the realm of possibility considering the dark history of this place.~
@124 = ~Long before Huros converted this place into an orphanage, the building stood abandoned. Long ago, a young family lived here. According to old legends, father went on a frenzy and murdered his wife and daughter, then disappeared as if Helm himself swept him off the face of Toril. Civilians believe majority of details are tweaked or highly exaggerated but no one knows the full story, hence uncertainty.~
@125 = ~I fear for my children's safety, both physical and psychological. Possibility of an undead creature did cross my mind. I'd be stupid to discard their concerns as youthful fantasies and imagination, especially in a world like this.~
@126 = ~I don't know what to do at this point.~
@127 = ~Have no fear. We will do our best to uncover the truth.~
@128 = ~Branwen, are you proficient with exorcisms?~
@129 = ~Yeslick, any advice on how we can deal with it?~
@130 = ~Viconia, are you proficient with exorcisms?~
@131 = ~Ajantis, any thoughts?~
@132 = ~I am not skilled in arts of ghost repelling. I'm sorry. I don't know how to help you.~
@133 = ~Thank you very much. You're most kind. If your investigation proves fortuitous, come back to me.~
@134 = ~I understand perfectly. Looks like I have no other choice but to speak to higher ranking members of the order.~
@135 = ~My gratitude is endless, friends.~
@136 = ~You're back. How is the investigation going? Did you find anything?~
@137 = ~Yes. I believe the flower upstairs in children's room is responsible. It seems to produce some lucid hallucinations. Tilda could smell the scent of this flower as her bed is directly next to it. During each phase, the flower caused collective delusion that drove the children to see things that weren't there.~
@138 = ~We identified the flower. It's Mourning Lace Flower which causes hallucinations. Where did you get that flower?~
@139 = ~Nothing yet.~
@140 = ~The Mourning Lace Flower. It was a gift from lunatic who fancied me. He used to come here every day and leave things by the door such as flowers or carved in stone figurines. He declared his obsessive love for me, and I rejected him instantly. That flower... it was his first gift.~
@141 = ~The Mourning Lace Flower. It was a gift from lunatic who fancied me. He used to come here every day and leave things by the door such as flowers or carved in stone figurines. He declared his obsessive love for me, and I rejected him instantly. That flower... it was his first gift.~
@142 = ~I didn't toss it away only because children insisted that it's pretty and compliments the interior. I conceded to their pleas. I wish I hadn't now that the truth came to light. I shall throw it away. Thank you so much for all your help. I appreciate your efforts. Here is some gold for your trouble.~
@143 = ~An exemplary calling, my lady. As a fellow Helmite, I commend your dedication. There is far too much misery in this world, and too few willing to stand against it.~
@144 = ~You're absolutely right, good paladin. Nasty times are upon us and we need to take care of one another, so benevolence overcomes malice.~
@145 = ~Daddy told me about this when I was younger, as means to creep me out and stop me from breaking out of the mansion at night. His rendition of the story might've been embellished for my sake, but if memory serves, the husband's behaviour started to deteriorate day by day. He refused to eat, drink, sleep and fell violently ill. His demeanor became cold and he distanced himself from his family. As time went on, he became more unrecognizable and aggressive. He would beat his son and threaten his wife.~
@146 = ~Eventually, he snapped. He murdered them both in cold blood. Their screams reached sympathetic ears out on the streets, and Watch members were called. They came across a massacre, while husband himself simply vanished. Chilling story with unsettled facts and details, but what the truth might've been nobody can say.~
@147 = ~<CHARNAME>, we should take a look at this. I cannot stand by when innocent children live in fear. They've been through enough already.~
@148 = ~It isn't our concern! Starvation is part of the nature. Natural selection! We are naught to disrupt the course of Mother Nature's volition.~
